From eac46efa8946b254501f12cdd91adf28218572c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:49:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 57/61] enigmata environment: Enigmata puzzles graded by the
 tasks' own verifiers

A native environment, so a run can mix it with the math and multiple-choice environments. Each row's ground truth is a JSON object {task, difficulty, answer, meta} from the Enigmata generator; the verifier of that task (imported from an Enigmata checkout, env.enigmata.repo_dir) grades the claim frame, or the reply when the claim is empty (fallback_frame). Verifiers run in Ray worker actors under a per-call alarm (timeout_s); exceptions and timeouts score 0 and are counted; a hung worker is replaced after hard_timeout_s. Optional per-sample stats file (stats_path).

---
